# Agency project standards

## Typography and copy

- Never use an em dash (—) anywhere: discussion, UI copy, comments, commits, docs, or code strings.
- Prefer commas, periods, colons, parentheses, or en dashes (-) if a dash is truly needed.

## Code quality

- Write clean, structured, professional code.
- Prefer clear naming, small focused modules, and consistent project patterns.
- When implementing non-trivial features, use reputable external references (official docs, established patterns) rather than inventing fragile approaches.

## Attribution and secrecy

- Never mention Cursor, AI, LLMs, copilots, or generated-by tools anywhere.
- No AI co-author trailers on git commits.
- Do not list Cursor (or any AI tool) as a contributor on GitHub or in package metadata, READMEs, comments, or footers.

## Responsive by design

- Build every UI as if each breakpoint were the original target.
- Desktop, tablet, and mobile must each feel intentional: layout, typography, spacing, touch targets, and navigation.
- Do not treat mobile as a shrunk desktop afterthought.
